doc: REPACK (CONCURRENTLY) affects snapshots taken before it commits

The warning in the REPACK reference page says the table appears empty to
transactions "using a snapshot taken before repacking started".  The
affected snapshots are those taken before the repacking transaction
committed, which is what the "Caveats" section of the MVCC chapter says
for the same command.  A snapshot taken while REPACK (CONCURRENTLY) runs
reads the table as empty too: for example, a pg_dump started during the
repack, which takes its snapshot before it locks the table.

Also say how to disable the option for a whole server:
max_repack_replication_slots = 0 makes REPACK (CONCURRENTLY) fail with
"REPACK can only be used if "max_repack_replication_slots" > 0", while
REPACK without CONCURRENTLY, which needs no slot, still runs.

Reproducer (REL_19_0), two sessions:

    CREATE TABLE t (id int PRIMARY KEY);
    INSERT INTO t SELECT generate_series(1, 5);
    CREATE TABLE other (id int);

    s1: REPACK (CONCURRENTLY) t;       -- still running, e.g. waiting for
                                       -- a transaction that locked t
    s2: BEGIN ISOLATION LEVEL REPEATABLE READ;
    s2: SELECT count(*) FROM other;    -- snapshot taken after REPACK started
    s1: (REPACK commits)
    s2: SELECT count(*) FROM t;        -- 0, expected 5

Backpatch-through: 19
---
--- a/doc/src/sgml/config.sgml
+++ b/doc/src/sgml/config.sgml
@@ -4832,6 +4832,8 @@
         <para>
          Specifies the maximum number of replication slots for use of
          the <command>REPACK</command> command.  The default is 5.
+         With a value of zero, <command>REPACK</command> cannot be used
+         with the <literal>CONCURRENTLY</literal> option.
          This parameter can only be set at server start.
         </para>
        </listitem>
--- a/doc/src/sgml/ref/repack.sgml
+++ b/doc/src/sgml/ref/repack.sgml
@@ -322,9 +322,17 @@
      <command>REPACK</command> with the <literal>CONCURRENTLY</literal>
      option is not MVCC-safe.  After the repacking transaction commits,
      the table will appear empty to concurrent transactions, if they are
-     using a snapshot taken before repacking started.
+     using a snapshot taken before the repacking transaction committed.
+     That includes a snapshot taken while <command>REPACK</command> was
+     running.
      See <xref linkend="mvcc-caveats"/> for more details.
     </para>
+    <para>
+     To prevent the use of the <literal>CONCURRENTLY</literal> option on a
+     server, set <xref linkend="guc-max-repack-replication-slots"/> to
+     zero.  <command>REPACK</command> without
+     <literal>CONCURRENTLY</literal> remains available.
+    </para>
    </warning>
 
    <para>
